import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.Cc8dJFaW.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-19 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-19 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-19.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-19.md","lastUpdated":null}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-19.md"};function o(s,e,l,c,p,d){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="_2026-11-19-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-19 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-19-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-19 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Core judgment: enterprise governance connects skill declarations, concrete identity/object versions, actual execution and external delivery evidence. Study Bulbasaur skill contracts and explicit evaluation, Codex child-local authority, Paperclip delivery gates and Orca cross-surface state authority.</p><p>Started 2026-11-19 10:47:09 Asia/Shanghai. Fresh main Registry: 47 researchers and 88 original repository entries. Deduplicated against run 2026-11-18T020523Z and published reports, with no fabricated missed-day reports. Event dates below are UTC. 57 observations, seven analyses; zero local experiments, articles, formal development reviews or external comments. Merges, releases, experimental flags and production availability are distinct.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><p><span id="o1"></span></p><h3 id="o1-mansura-habiba-declared-side-effects-constrain-permissions" tabindex="-1">O1 Mansura Habiba: declared side effects constrain permissions <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-mansura-habiba-declared-side-effects-constrain-permissions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 Mansura Habiba: declared side effects constrain permissions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #25, authored by Mansura Habiba. A shared operation-cost table checks permissions against risk.side_effects; SideEffectCeiling/PermissionsHook deny excess operations and append audit records. Regex-bounded commands remain unverified read-only claims, and the full hook bus is excluded. This author-related project is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli/pull/25" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T15:07:59Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a></p><p><span id="o2"></span></p><h3 id="o2-bulbasaur-exposes-transport-neutral-skill-assessment" tabindex="-1">O2 Bulbasaur exposes transport-neutral skill assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-bulbasaur-exposes-transport-neutral-skill-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 Bulbasaur exposes transport-neutral skill assessment&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #26. Independent api/ serves REST validation/assessment and MCP over one static compiler service, recording SHA-256 of exact SKILL.md bytes. Behavioral evaluation defaults to not_run. OAC work is a read-only mock/candidate schema, not Catalog approval or completed upstream integration. REST uses its own bearer token; MCP is loopback-only. Apache-2.0 verified; api/README documents uv startup, not performed locally.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli/pull/26" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T12:55:26Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a></p><p><span id="o3"></span></p><h3 id="o3-bulbasaur-adds-explicitly-opted-in-behavioral-evaluation" tabindex="-1">O3 Bulbasaur adds explicitly opted-in behavioral evaluation <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-bulbasaur-adds-explicitly-opted-in-behavioral-evaluation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 Bulbasaur adds explicitly opted-in behavioral evaluation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #29. Assessment accepts evaluation under operator-owned runtime allowlists/case limits and returns v2 evidence only on explicit runs; static v1 stays default. Mock/heuristic defaults exercise machinery, not real skill effectiveness. Opted-in Ollama remains development-only without hard isolation/timeouts. No skill-script execution or Pi/Gantry integration. Stale draft wording does not override the merged API state.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli/pull/29" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T13:40:45Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a></p><p><span id="o4"></span></p><h3 id="o4-mcp-typescript-sdk-merges-experimental-extensions-and-middleware" tabindex="-1">O4 MCP TypeScript SDK merges experimental extensions and middleware <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-mcp-typescript-sdk-merges-experimental-extensions-and-middleware" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 MCP TypeScript SDK merges experimental extensions and middleware&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #2820. Client/server extensions use id + setup(ctx), dependencies, custom handlers and incoming-request middleware. Duplicate IDs, missing dependencies and handler replacement fail. Extension middleware wraps later application middleware. Notifications/outgoing middleware are excluded and low-level Server is unchanged. APIs remain experimental and may change in minor releases; this is not a new specification release.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2820" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:47:53Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o5"></span></p><h3 id="o5-mcp-sdk-backfills-text-for-content-less-structured-results" tabindex="-1">O5 MCP SDK backfills text for content-less structured results <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-mcp-sdk-backfills-text-for-content-less-structured-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 MCP SDK backfills text for content-less structured results&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #3153. structuredContent without content gets serialized JSON text for content-only clients; explicit content:[] stays empty. Mixed result-family payloads remain rejected. The cited new conformance scenario is not yet part of a released conformance suite.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/3153" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T17:31:45Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o6"></span></p><h3 id="o6-mcp-sdk-makes-internal-diagnostics-injectable" tabindex="-1">O6 MCP SDK makes internal diagnostics injectable <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-mcp-sdk-makes-internal-diagnostics-injectable" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 MCP SDK makes internal diagnostics injectable&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #2370. SDK logging can be injected into clients, servers, handlers and OAuth providers, separating diagnostics from stdio JSON-RPC. Custom OAuth providers use sdkLogger. Logger errors are ignored; default remains console. Redaction/filtering remains the host logger&#39;s responsibility.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2370" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:20:09Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o7"></span></p><h3 id="o7-github-mcp-server-adds-doubly-gated-pr-artifact-tools" tabindex="-1">O7 GitHub MCP Server adds doubly gated PR artifact tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-github-mcp-server-adds-doubly-gated-pr-artifact-tools" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 GitHub MCP Server adds doubly gated PR artifact tools&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #3843. Experimental PR artifact list/upsert/delete tools default off. MCP feature opt-in is separate from GitHub&#39;s repository API rollout gate; read-only mode omits writes and lockdown rejects operations. Upstream scratch-repository testing did not exercise rollout toggling or independently verify exact fine-grained permission mappings.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/3843" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T15:33:22Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o8"></span></p><h3 id="o8-github-cli-offers-runnable-event-waiting-under-preview-access" tabindex="-1">O8 GitHub CLI offers runnable event waiting under preview access <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-github-cli-offers-runnable-event-waiting-under-preview-access" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 GitHub CLI offers runnable event waiting under preview access&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Official November 18: gh 2.105.0 adds gh event listen, creating subscriptions and emitting JSON lines. It exits on the first event by default, with count/follow/timeout, covering reviews, head/state changes and completed checks. Commands/Event Streams remain preview with waitlist access. This is new CLI delivery after yesterday&#39;s stream announcement, not proof of replay or exactly-once.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-18-wait-for-pull-request-events-with-github-cli/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OFFICIAL_ANNOUNCEMENT · 2026-11-18</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o9"></span></p><h3 id="o9-copilot-team-plugin-defaults-reach-ga" tabindex="-1">O9 Copilot team plugin defaults reach GA <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-copilot-team-plugin-defaults-reach-ga" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 Copilot team plugin defaults reach GA&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Official November 18 GA for Business/Enterprise. Maintainers/owners select plugins defaulted for direct team members; child teams do not inherit, and members can disable them where policy allows. Enterprise/organization required/blocked plugins and marketplaces take precedence. High learning value; increased attention to enterprise role-capability distribution.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-18-customize-github-copilot-for-your-team/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OFFICIAL_ANNOUNCEMENT · 2026-11-18</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o10"></span></p><h3 id="o10-copilot-connector-expansion-retains-administrative-admission" tabindex="-1">O10 Copilot connector expansion retains administrative admission <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-copilot-connector-expansion-retains-administrative-admission" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 Copilot connector expansion retains administrative admission&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Official November 18 public-preview expansion adds eight connectors including Supabase, Box, Calendly and Buildkite across App/CLI/VS Code. Business/Enterprise needs preview policy, explicit MCP allowlists need additions, and some providers need their own admin enablement. Study admission and reuse; catalog presence does not establish organizational access.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-18-connect-supabase-box-calendly-and-more-to-copilot/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OFFICIAL_ANNOUNCEMENT · 2026-11-18</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o11"></span></p><h3 id="o11-codex-separates-inherited-context-from-child-authorization" tabindex="-1">O11 Codex separates inherited context from child authorization <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-codex-separates-inherited-context-from-child-authorization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 Codex separates inherited context from child authorization&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62314. Prepared forks may inherit root session ID and ancestor conversation context, but exclude ancestor authorization evidence at startup, resume and sender-evidence reconstruction. Child-local evidence remains; disabled-plugin settings still inherit. This constrains authorization attribution across delegation.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62314" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:37:38Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o12"></span></p><h3 id="o12-codex-supports-per-tool-approval-reviewers" tabindex="-1">O12 Codex supports per-tool approval reviewers <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-codex-supports-per-tool-approval-reviewers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 Codex supports per-tool approval reviewers&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62360. Per-app-tool approvals_reviewer overrides account/app/session defaults subject to managed requirements. Matching uses raw name then title; it covers tool approvals and MCP requests tied to verified app invocation. Same-name tools are not thereby authenticated.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62360" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T20:42:50Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o13"></span></p><h3 id="o13-codex-guardian-catches-up-evidence-before-action-review" tabindex="-1">O13 Codex Guardian catches up evidence before action review <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-codex-guardian-catches-up-evidence-before-action-review" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 Codex Guardian catches up evidence before action review&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18. #62309/#62310 catch up subscribed evidence before synchronous review, check captured authorization before/after verdict and block preparation failures under one deadline. #62373&#39;s optional in-memory SQLite board leaves attached review unavailable on cold root resume; disk remains default. Enabled denial reconsideration (#62374) allows one extra sample, retaining the first denial/reason if it times out.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62309" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:18:30Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62310" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:19:06Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62373" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:58:08Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62374" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:58:46Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o14"></span></p><h3 id="o14-codex-pauses-telemetry-only-sandbox-integrity-checks" tabindex="-1">O14 Codex pauses telemetry-only sandbox integrity checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-codex-pauses-telemetry-only-sandbox-integrity-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 Codex pauses telemetry-only sandbox integrity checks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 19, #62389. Shared exec-server/legacy launch stops telemetry-only integrity discovery, preparation and reporting because it duplicates enforcement preparation. Related launch integration cases are ignored while isolated checker tests remain. This change does not establish that sandbox enforcement is disabled.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62389" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T01:16:40Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o15"></span></p><h3 id="o15-codex-persists-queued-child-replies-before-parent-abortion" tabindex="-1">O15 Codex persists queued child replies before parent abortion <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-codex-persists-queued-child-replies-before-parent-abortion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 Codex persists queued child replies before parent abortion&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62348. Interruption now persists and flushes acknowledged-but-unconsumed child replies before TurnAborted, including when interruption markers are disabled. Upstream regression requires one occurrence in the next inference request. No corresponding local CodeFlowMu behavior was tested.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62348" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T19:40:16Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o16"></span></p><h3 id="o16-codex-records-trace-reduction-boundaries-and-timing-gaps" tabindex="-1">O16 Codex records trace-reduction boundaries and timing gaps <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-codex-records-trace-reduction-boundaries-and-timing-gaps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 Codex records trace-reduction boundaries and timing gaps&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18–19, #62357/#62407. Incomplete critical paths name missing starts, unattributed waits, forced teardown and other causes. Encoded strings at least 64 KiB are deduplicated; complete captures reconstruct bytes. Budgets can still omit payloads, distinguishing missing from null while preserving surviving terminal metadata/output IDs. Reduced traces are not complete evidence.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62357" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T20:30:31Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62407" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T02:41:31Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o17"></span></p><h3 id="o17-codex-preserves-resumed-permissions-and-cross-platform-roots" tabindex="-1">O17 Codex preserves resumed permissions and cross-platform roots <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-codex-preserves-resumed-permissions-and-cross-platform-roots" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 Codex preserves resumed permissions and cross-platform roots&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62194/#62376/#62377. Resumed codex exec preserves saved sandbox restrictions; writable/workspace roots retain source-platform path semantics across OS boundaries. These are recovery/adapter changes, not local acceptance of every platform combination.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62194" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T05:14:25Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62376" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T22:40:00Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62377" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T22:40:38Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a></p><p><span id="o18"></span></p><h3 id="o18-codex-0-170-delivers-previously-merged-changes" tabindex="-1">O18 Codex 0.170 delivers previously merged changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-codex-0-170-delivers-previously-merged-changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 Codex 0.170 delivers previously merged changes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>rust-v0.170.0 RELEASED November 18 at 03:40 UTC after yesterday&#39;s cutoff. Notes include MCP OAuth cancellation/login/logout races, Cloud reconnect, child restrictions and Windows permission/recovery fixes. The new event is delivery, not re-counting earlier merges; today&#39;s Guardian merges are not assumed included.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.170.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T03:40:48Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o19"></span></p><h3 id="o19-claude-code-2-1-328-changes-hook-failure-and-audit-stages" tabindex="-1">O19 Claude Code 2.1.328 changes hook failure and audit stages <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-claude-code-2-1-328-changes-hook-failure-and-audit-stages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 Claude Code 2.1.328 changes hook failure and audit stages&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 19. mcp_tool hooks support onFailure:block, and hosts can prohibit resuming hook-deferred tool calls. Code Mode output no longer triggers UserPromptSubmit; redaction moves to PostToolUse updatedToolOutput. Pre-execution refusals no longer invoke managed PostToolUse. Recheck audit/redaction bindings rather than interpreting absent logs as absence of an attempt.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.328" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-19T01:14:04Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o20"></span></p><h3 id="o20-claude-code-hardens-self-hosted-recovery-interpretation" tabindex="-1">O20 Claude Code hardens self-hosted recovery interpretation <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-claude-code-hardens-self-hosted-recovery-interpretation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 Claude Code hardens self-hosted recovery interpretation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The same v2.1.328 release fixes stopping all sessions on a proxy&#39;s HTTP200/empty-object response, deleting kept clone data after temporary disk errors, and missing deregistration reasons after registered startup failures. Non-fork subagents under the stated configuration wait for their own children; resumed sessions check prior work still exists. Upstream release claims, not local reproduction.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.328" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-19T01:14:04Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a></p><p><span id="o21"></span></p><h3 id="o21-gemini-cli-ties-shell-decisions-to-executable-arguments" tabindex="-1">O21 Gemini CLI ties shell decisions to executable arguments <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-gemini-cli-ties-shell-decisions-to-executable-arguments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 Gemini CLI ties shell decisions to executable arguments&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #30338/#30355. Unresolved Bash expansion retains ASK_USER, including parse failure; explicit allow rules remain and that change excludes PowerShell. Prefix/regex rules anchor to the top-level command with scoped alternation. Nested fields and pre-expansion text must not substitute for checked command arguments.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30338" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T19:39:26Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30355" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:21:44Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a></p><p><span id="o22"></span></p><h3 id="o22-langgraph-propagates-state-overrides-into-tool-runtime" tabindex="-1">O22 LangGraph propagates state overrides into tool runtime <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-langgraph-propagates-state-overrides-into-tool-runtime" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 LangGraph propagates state overrides into tool runtime&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #9730. override(state=...) now updates runtime.state as well as the request, reaching InjectedState, ToolRuntime and inner wrappers. Explicit state wins over a stale supplied runtime. Pre-action control needs verification of what the tool actually reads.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9730" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:33:00Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o23"></span></p><h3 id="o23-langchain-labels-synthetic-hitl-tool-messages" tabindex="-1">O23 LangChain labels synthetic HITL tool messages <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-langchain-labels-synthetic-hitl-tool-messages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 LangChain labels synthetic HITL tool messages&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #41928, delivered in langchain 1.5.2. Synthetic rejection/human-response ToolMessages carry lc_source and decision; real outputs after approved/edited execution stay untagged. Metadata identifies provenance, not trust or authorization.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/41928" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:41:09Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/releases/tag/langchain%3D%3D1.5.2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T22:30:43Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o24"></span></p><h3 id="o24-langchain-isolates-async-clients-across-model-instances" tabindex="-1">O24 LangChain isolates async clients across model instances <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-langchain-isolates-async-clients-across-model-instances" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 LangChain isolates async clients across model instances&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #41944, released in langchain-openai 1.8.2. Each model owns its async HTTP client while SSL configuration is shared, avoiding connections tied to another closed event loop. Reusing one model across loops remains unsupported, and per-request model creation may open more connections.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/41944" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:41:45Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/releases/tag/langchain-openai%3D%3D1.8.2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T16:53:05Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a5">A5</a></p><p><span id="o25"></span></p><h3 id="o25-crewai-1-15-42-changes-default-knowledge-storage" tabindex="-1">O25 CrewAI 1.15.42 changes default knowledge storage <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-crewai-1-15-42-changes-default-knowledge-storage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 CrewAI 1.15.42 changes default knowledge storage&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED/RELEASED November 18, #8941/1.15.42. Chroma becomes optional and default knowledge/search uses local Qdrant. Old Chroma collections are neither read nor migrated. Default per-process storage is removed at exit and re-embedded next run; fixed local paths admit one process, requiring a server or Chroma for sharing. Default embeddings remain OpenAI, so local storage is not offline inference.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/8941" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T14:56:52Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/releases/tag/1.15.42" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T16:38:31Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a5">A5</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o26"></span></p><h3 id="o26-crewai-gives-shared-default-flow-instances-distinct-run-ids" tabindex="-1">O26 CrewAI gives shared-default Flow instances distinct run IDs <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-crewai-gives-shared-default-flow-instances-distinct-run-ids" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 CrewAI gives shared-default Flow instances distinct run IDs&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #9499, included in 1.15.42. A class-level initial_state=S() reused a generated ID and persisted separate runs under one flow_uuid. The fix regenerates factory IDs for shared defaults while preserving explicit IDs and passed-in resume state. Intentional continuation remains distinct from accidental run merging.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9499" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T05:23:53Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/releases/tag/1.15.42" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T16:38:31Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a5">A5</a></p><p><span id="o27"></span></p><h3 id="o27-crewai-standalone-kickoff-timeout-fix-remains-open" tabindex="-1">O27 CrewAI standalone kickoff timeout fix remains open <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-crewai-standalone-kickoff-timeout-fix-remains-open" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 CrewAI standalone kickoff timeout fix remains open&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Created November 18, #9539 remains OPEN, not draft or merged. It proposes enforcing max_execution_time for standalone kickoff/kickoff_async; its author explicitly could not run the new tests. The older execute_task fix shipped in 1.15.42 reports timeout promptly but cannot kill an already-running Python thread. These paths and stopping effects are separate; #9324 is not counted as a new merge.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9539" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OPEN · 2026-11-18T09:42:45Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9324" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-16T16:53:26Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/releases/tag/1.15.42" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T16:38:31Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a></p><p><span id="o28"></span></p><h3 id="o28-paperclip-gates-task-completion-on-merged-pr-deliverables" tabindex="-1">O28 Paperclip gates task completion on merged PR deliverables <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-paperclip-gates-task-completion-on-merged-pr-deliverables" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 Paperclip gates task completion on merged PR deliverables&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 19, #22244, after this cycle&#39;s stable release. Declared delivery PRs must be verified merged by GitHub; open/draft/closed-unmerged/unavailable/malformed outputs cannot complete a task, nor can agent-written merge claims. Current deliverables are rechecked under lock, remote reads outside the transaction; review can start earlier. High learning/delivery-governance attention; main radar unchanged.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22244" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T00:20:18Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o29"></span></p><h3 id="o29-paperclip-distinguishes-runner-recovery-task-locks-and-futile-retries" tabindex="-1">O29 Paperclip distinguishes runner recovery, task locks and futile retries <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-paperclip-distinguishes-runner-recovery-task-locks-and-futile-retries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 Paperclip distinguishes runner recovery, task locks and futile retries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Three November 18 merges: #22235 permits one same-conversation continuation for an in-flight turn lost on runner restore; #22239 marks run-epoch sandbox_disk_full and stops retries into equally sized sandboxes; #22248 retains task locks while the executor settles a terminal run, preserving scheduled usage-limit retries. Yesterday&#39;s disk reserve did not establish turn/task recovery. High learning value and increased recovery attention.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22235" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:55:16Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22239" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:19:13Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22248" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:39:15Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a5">A5</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o30"></span></p><h3 id="o30-paperclip-connects-company-workload-identity-to-aws-credentials" tabindex="-1">O30 Paperclip connects company workload identity to AWS credentials <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-paperclip-connects-company-workload-identity-to-aws-credentials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 Paperclip connects company workload identity to AWS credentials&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22083/#22195. Per-company signing keys, issuer/JWKS and rotation audit support connection-scoped tokens. The experimentally gated AWS connector mints role/key sessions with read-only session policies, cache and in-flight deduplication. A 401 evicts/remints credentials but requires explicit retry, avoiding action replay. The identity foundation initially had no consumer; AWS supplies the later integration. High enterprise-identity learning/attention.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22083" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T05:33:48Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22195" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T18:48:50Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o31"></span></p><h3 id="o31-paperclip-preserves-the-manual-routine-caller" tabindex="-1">O31 Paperclip preserves the manual routine caller <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-paperclip-preserves-the-manual-routine-caller" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 Paperclip preserves the manual routine caller&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22177. A Run now dispatch could read before its routine-run transaction committed and fall back to the saved owner&#39;s account. The selected responsible caller now travels in wake context while routine ownership stays unchanged. Upstream PostgreSQL/heartbeat before-after evidence is not local reproduction. High learning value for cross-user execution identity.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22177" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T15:03:59Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o32"></span></p><h3 id="o32-paperclip-gates-connector-use-on-installation-and-pinned-aliases" tabindex="-1">O32 Paperclip gates connector use on installation and pinned aliases <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-paperclip-gates-connector-use-on-installation-and-pinned-aliases" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 Paperclip gates connector use on installation and pinned aliases&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22237/#22213. Plugin connectors require an agent/company install before grants/trust/allow checks; direct-name calls cannot bypass it. Unique display/gateway names can resolve to pinned authorized aliases while fresh-grant/work-mode filtering remains; ambiguous matches fail. High learning value and increased authorization-coverage attention; main radar unchanged.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22237" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:34:10Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22213" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:24:46Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o33"></span></p><h3 id="o33-paperclip-removes-claude-mcp-bearer-tokens-from-argv" tabindex="-1">O33 Paperclip removes Claude MCP bearer tokens from argv <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-paperclip-removes-claude-mcp-bearer-tokens-from-argv" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 Paperclip removes Claude MCP bearer tokens from argv&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22206. Inline --mcp-config bearer tokens could enter tool logs through ps. Claude ACPX now receives environment-variable references expanded by Claude. Other ACPX agents retain literal headers without known expansion support; environment storage is not secrecy from same-privilege code. High learning value; continue credential-boundary watch.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22206" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:58:47Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a></p><p><span id="o34"></span></p><h3 id="o34-paperclip-bounds-online-durable-data-migration-passes" tabindex="-1">O34 Paperclip bounds online durable-data migration passes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o34-paperclip-bounds-online-durable-data-migration-passes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O34 Paperclip bounds online durable-data migration passes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22240. With S3/durable-file prerequisites, a 60-second online pass moves agent files, skills and runtime backups, defers busy items and reports progress/configuration blockers with existing claims/CAS around writers. Zero-maintenance-window volume-free enrollment is the objective, not verified completion across deployments. High delivery learning value; trial maturity.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22240" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:36:31Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o35"></span></p><h3 id="o35-paperclip-stable-release-changes-connector-availability" tabindex="-1">O35 Paperclip stable release changes connector availability <a class="header-anchor" href="#o35-paperclip-stable-release-changes-connector-availability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O35 Paperclip stable release changes connector availability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>v2026.1117.0 was RELEASED November 18 at 22:20 UTC, distinct from the notes&#39; November 17 label. Existing Coordinator/Agent Chat/recovery work ships here. Built-in Google Workspace defaults off pending verification, including old connections, unless explicitly enabled experimentally. Historical 1,586 commits are not daily new events, and later completion-gate merges are not assumed packaged. High delivery attention; main radar retained, MIT verified.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/releases/tag/v2026.1117.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-18T22:20:29Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o36"></span></p><h3 id="o36-orca-binds-phone-merges-to-the-reviewed-pr-head" tabindex="-1">O36 Orca binds phone merges to the reviewed PR head <a class="header-anchor" href="#o36-orca-binds-phone-merges-to-the-reviewed-pr-head" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O36 Orca binds phone merges to the reviewed PR head&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 19, #44354. Phone merges submit expectedHeadSha, checked against a fresh PR and fenced again at merge. New pushes after screen load force refresh. High mobile-approval learning/attention, second circle unchanged; no real-phone trial.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44354" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T00:22:34Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o37"></span></p><h3 id="o37-orca-refuses-unsafe-workspace-and-remote-host-fallbacks" tabindex="-1">O37 Orca refuses unsafe workspace and remote-host fallbacks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o37-orca-refuses-unsafe-workspace-and-remote-host-fallbacks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O37 Orca refuses unsafe workspace and remote-host fallbacks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18–19, #44237/#43958. Chat-agent browser commands outside a resolved workspace without page fail instead of taking the user&#39;s active tab; analogous terminal/computer fallback exposure is outside that fix. Paired-host launches that would use desktop full-access settings are refused. High cross-host governance learning/attention; circle unchanged.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44237" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T02:28:59Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43958" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T07:16:43Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o38"></span></p><h3 id="o38-orca-proves-resource-release-and-reports-idle-provider-death" tabindex="-1">O38 Orca proves resource release and reports idle provider death <a class="header-anchor" href="#o38-orca-proves-resource-release-and-reports-idle-provider-death" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O38 Orca proves resource release and reports idle provider death&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18–19, #43953/#43955. Proven stop plus preserved output reference releases worker terminals atomically; legacy stuck rows are reclaimed only with exited-incarnation proof, not offline/unknown hosts. Idle provider death now reports fenced exits to open Dispatches so coordinators do not wait forever. High lifecycle learning/attention.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43953" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T02:03:56Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43955" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T20:18:19Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o39"></span></p><h3 id="o39-orca-repairs-child-approval-evidence-and-completion-projection" tabindex="-1">O39 Orca repairs child approval evidence and completion projection <a class="header-anchor" href="#o39-orca-repairs-child-approval-evidence-and-completion-projection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O39 Orca repairs child approval evidence and completion projection&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18–19, #44302/#43858/#44375. Escalation briefly waits for the actual child permission dialog, coordinator approval reasons reach workers with receipts, and paired clients keep Pi roots working while children remain. High learning value for evidence availability versus lifecycle completion.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44302" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:04:10Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43858" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T03:04:13Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44375" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T01:02:11Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o40"></span></p><h3 id="o40-orca-negotiates-peer-mail-while-retaining-home-authority" tabindex="-1">O40 Orca negotiates peer mail while retaining home authority <a class="header-anchor" href="#o40-orca-negotiates-peer-mail-while-retaining-home-authority" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O40 Orca negotiates peer mail while retaining home authority&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #44034. Paired servers carry ordinary status/handoff/question/dispatch/merge_ready mail, negotiating peer-mail-types.v1 before new types and explicitly refusing unsupported sends. Dispatch-changing escalation/decision_gate/worker_done/heartbeat remain on the Run home with authority checks. High learning value for separating messaging interoperability from state authority.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44034" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:23:29Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a6">A6</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o41"></span></p><h3 id="o41-orca-makes-phone-command-and-setup-boundaries-explicit" tabindex="-1">O41 Orca makes phone command and setup boundaries explicit <a class="header-anchor" href="#o41-orca-makes-phone-command-and-setup-boundaries-explicit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O41 Orca makes phone command and setup boundaries explicit&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18–19, #44250/#43978. Structured phone chats implement /fork and /usage, mark /resume and /btw desktop-only rather than send them as plain agent text, and can wait for project setup before launch. Scope excludes terminal chats and projects without setup. Stale held-for-review prose is not current PR status. Medium-high learning value; second-circle mobile watch.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/44250" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T02:31:32Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43978" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T22:43:14Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o42"></span></p><h3 id="o42-orca-bounds-snapshot-delivery-and-history-catch-up" tabindex="-1">O42 Orca bounds snapshot delivery and history catch-up <a class="header-anchor" href="#o42-orca-bounds-snapshot-delivery-and-history-catch-up" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O42 Orca bounds snapshot delivery and history catch-up&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #43456. Subscribers deliver once at a time, coalescing pending live text/catch-ups without crossing ordered operations; history reads bound outstanding work as well as active workers. Journal writes, cursors and fences retain semantics. High long-running memory learning value; no local load test.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43456" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:34:21Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a5">A5</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o43"></span></p><h3 id="o43-orca-persists-remote-browser-logins-across-restart" tabindex="-1">O43 Orca persists remote browser logins across restart <a class="header-anchor" href="#o43-orca-persists-remote-browser-logins-across-restart" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O43 Orca persists remote browser logins across restart&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #43956. SSH/This-device route partitions preserve sealed session-cookie snapshots restored before first load; This-device adds password save/fill. Continuity adds product value and a credential-persistence boundary to examine. No local cross-user/host isolation test; medium-high product attention, circle unchanged.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43956" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:54:32Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o44"></span></p><h3 id="o44-beads-adds-transactional-claim-checks-and-complete-claim-audit-paths" tabindex="-1">O44 Beads adds transactional claim checks and complete claim audit paths <a class="header-anchor" href="#o44-beads-adds-transactional-claim-checks-and-complete-claim-audit-paths" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O44 Beads adds transactional claim checks and complete claim audit paths&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #8360/#8336/#8024. Claims check local blockers transactionally with a separate explicit force override. With audit.enabled, direct/proxy claim and claim-next paths reach the sidecar. Event old_value becomes the changed fields&#39; pre-image; paths lacking prior state do not invent it. High learning value for claim contracts and evidence; retain main radar study.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8360" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T19:20:28Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8336" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T20:07:41Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8024" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T13:35:27Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o45"></span></p><h3 id="o45-beads-requires-consent-and-identity-checks-at-data-boundaries" tabindex="-1">O45 Beads requires consent and identity checks at data boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#o45-beads-requires-consent-and-identity-checks-at-data-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O45 Beads requires consent and identity checks at data boundaries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #8353/#8475. Adopting Dolt history from git origin now defaults to no, with explicit choice required non-interactively. Plain proxied workspaces explicitly selecting another database get a read-only project-identity check before attach/migration. This is not a new universal strict check on every open. High learning value for project contamination/deployment boundaries.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8353" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T19:37:52Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8475" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T15:42:06Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o46"></span></p><h3 id="o46-beads-clears-rolled-back-ids-and-remints-replayed-imports" tabindex="-1">O46 Beads clears rolled-back IDs and remints replayed imports <a class="header-anchor" href="#o46-beads-clears-rolled-back-ids-and-remints-replayed-imports" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O46 Beads clears rolled-back IDs and remints replayed imports&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #8470/#8464. Rolled-back creates clear generated caller-visible IDs, while replayed proxied imports remint unset IDs instead of treating an uncommitted prior attempt as an existing object. High learning value for artifact identity versus commit receipts; no local comparison.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8470" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T20:10:43Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8464" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T15:55:58Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o47"></span></p><h3 id="o47-beads-names-schema-drift-without-claiming-automatic-rollback" tabindex="-1">O47 Beads names schema drift without claiming automatic rollback <a class="header-anchor" href="#o47-beads-names-schema-drift-without-claiming-automatic-rollback" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O47 Beads names schema drift without claiming automatic rollback&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #8361. Specific schema-encoding drift becomes a typed error naming migration/cursor/runbook. It stops on first error without skipping, retrying or rollback; partial uncommitted changes may remain and raw engine panics are not intercepted. High migration learning value, continuing yesterday&#39;s RC watch; MIT verified.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/8361" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T18:11:03Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o48"></span></p><h3 id="o48-openhands-records-inter-conversation-sender-provenance" tabindex="-1">O48 OpenHands records inter-conversation sender provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#o48-openhands-records-inter-conversation-sender-provenance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O48 OpenHands records inter-conversation sender provenance&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #6960/#6975. REST sends/initial messages and child tasks preserve conversation sender provenance, with inter-conversation text explicitly not approving for the user. Hooks/visualizers can use sender; the main App frontend does not yet read it. Non-user run-confirmation guards are a separate follow-up, not a completed authorization loop.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6960" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T19:21:06Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6975" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T23:26:51Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o49"></span></p><h3 id="o49-openhands-isolates-lock-waiters-from-tool-execution" tabindex="-1">O49 OpenHands isolates lock waiters from tool execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#o49-openhands-isolates-lock-waiters-from-tool-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O49 OpenHands isolates lock waiters from tool execution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #6554. Tool execution holding a state lock and requests waiting on it shared the default executor; client pressure could exhaust threads and wedge service while /alive stayed green. Dedicated sequential-tool/per-conversation state executors and off-loop replay address it. Upstream mechanism reviewed; not load-tested locally.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6554" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T17:43:32Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a4">A4</a></p><p><span id="o50"></span></p><h3 id="o50-openhands-gives-model-routers-explicit-switching-state" tabindex="-1">O50 OpenHands gives model routers explicit switching state <a class="header-anchor" href="#o50-openhands-gives-model-routers-explicit-switching-state" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O50 OpenHands gives model routers explicit switching state&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 19, #6789/#6835. RouterLLM owns automatic/manual selection state with status/switch/resume APIs and runtime route addition, wrapping a plain LLM as needed. REST and Python/TypeScript clients are included. Upstream downstream manual testing is not local evidence or proof of arbitrary model-context compatibility.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6789" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T00:07:42Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6835" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-19T00:07:43Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a5">A5</a></p><p><span id="o51"></span></p><h3 id="o51-openhands-merges-a-resolution-judge-without-a-mainline-caller" tabindex="-1">O51 OpenHands merges a resolution judge without a mainline caller <a class="header-anchor" href="#o51-openhands-merges-a-resolution-judge-without-a-mainline-caller" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O51 OpenHands merges a resolution judge without a mainline caller&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #6962. A named resolution_judge LLM profile answers narrow yes/no questions, combined in code into resolved or outstanding answer/review/decision/check/unfinished/unclear states with its own retries/deadline. It explicitly has no caller on main yet, so automatic product acceptance is not established. Candidate for independent acceptance study.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6962" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T18:00:48Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o52"></span></p><h3 id="o52-langfuse-separates-user-key-budgets-and-live-defaults" tabindex="-1">O52 Langfuse separates user/key budgets and live defaults <a class="header-anchor" href="#o52-langfuse-separates-user-key-budgets-and-live-defaults" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O52 Langfuse separates user/key budgets and live defaults&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #20323/#20377/#20440. Key/user budgets have calendar intervals and live per-subject defaults rather than copied rows. Own key budgets can replace key defaults; administrators need user limits to cap a person&#39;s total. Enforcement/control plane is merged while the page remains PR-preview/staging-only. Production UI rollout and concurrent overspend boundaries were not locally established.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20323" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T10:33:42Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20377" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T17:50:52Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20440" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T18:59:33Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a5">A5</a></p><p><span id="o53"></span></p><h3 id="o53-langfuse-binds-bedrock-role-access-to-tenant-external-ids" tabindex="-1">O53 Langfuse binds Bedrock role access to tenant external IDs <a class="header-anchor" href="#o53-langfuse-binds-bedrock-role-access-to-tenant-external-ids" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O53 Langfuse binds Bedrock role access to tenant external IDs&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #20379. Customer IAM roles use a cross-account chain and server-generated project/organization-bound external IDs against confused-deputy access. Self-hosting needs cross-account role setup; public upsert and non-entitled organizations still reject role configuration. Study credential/tenant binding, not universal credential-free access.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20379" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T16:57:56Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a2">A2</a> · <a href="#a5">A5</a></p><p><span id="o54"></span></p><h3 id="o54-langfuse-handles-modern-mcp-and-clarifies-replacement-contracts" tabindex="-1">O54 Langfuse handles modern MCP and clarifies replacement contracts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o54-langfuse-handles-modern-mcp-and-clarifies-replacement-contracts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O54 Langfuse handles modern MCP and clarifies replacement contracts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #20384/#20418. Requests select modern or legacy MCP handling by the 2026 envelope with protocol-era telemetry, retaining legacy clients. Separately, updateEvaluator descriptions now state full replacement and clearing of omitted optional fields; on-wire schemas were already correct. Study alignment of wire contract, model-visible guidance and writes.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20384" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T08:48:50Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20418" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T09:45:11Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a1">A1</a> · <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><p><span id="o55"></span></p><h3 id="o55-phoenix-documents-validation-of-tasks-and-verifiers" tabindex="-1">O55 Phoenix documents validation of tasks and verifiers <a class="header-anchor" href="#o55-phoenix-documents-validation-of-tasks-and-verifiers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O55 Phoenix documents validation of tasks and verifiers&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #17821, with guidance delivered in next-day 21.2.1. Drawing on upstream Harbor experience, it defines outcome-based success, avoids grading hints, validates verifiers with oracle/nop controls and separates crashes/wrong answers from evaluation failures. Reusable guidance/examples, not a new benchmark score or local experiment.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/pull/17821" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T21:17:13Z</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/arize-phoenix-v21.2.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASED · 2026-11-19T01:26:55Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a3">A3</a></p><p><span id="o56"></span></p><h3 id="o56-orkas-preserves-utf-8-across-long-command-output-chunks" tabindex="-1">O56 Orkas preserves UTF-8 across long-command output chunks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o56-orkas-preserves-utf-8-across-long-command-output-chunks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O56 Orkas preserves UTF-8 across long-command output chunks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #228. Incremental per-pipe stdout/stderr decoding preserves split UTF-8 characters while retaining byte accounting, bounded output, cancellation and terminal receipts. Upstream measurements are not native Windows latency guarantees; not installed locally. Medium-high learning value for Chinese delivery evidence; main radar retained, MIT verified.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/228" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MERGED · 2026-11-18T14:41:55Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a6">A6</a> · <a href="#a7">A7</a></p><p><span id="o57"></span></p><h3 id="o57-adk-removes-the-visual-builder-assistant-and-built-in-agents" tabindex="-1">O57 ADK removes the visual builder assistant and built-in agents <a class="header-anchor" href="#o57-adk-removes-the-visual-builder-assistant-and-built-in-agents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O57 ADK removes the visual builder assistant and built-in agents&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Committed November 19: the removed visual builder&#39;s __adk_agent_builder_assistant, tools and built-in loading mechanism are deleted. Double-underscore names are reserved/rejected with API 404 rather than falling through to user agent directories. Mainline compatibility change for dependent development integrations, not project discontinuation.</p><p>Original evidence and state: <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/e2a21ac23260d043bf9d217b573af1bef48f0f70" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">COMMITTED · 2026-11-19T01:04:21Z</a></p><p>Research mapping: <a href="#a6">A6</a></p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><p><span id="a1"></span></p><h3 id="a1-skill-trust-spans-declaration-actual-arguments-control-and-behavior" tabindex="-1">A1 Skill trust spans declaration, actual arguments, control and behavior <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-skill-trust-spans-declaration-actual-arguments-control-and-behavior" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 Skill trust spans declaration, actual arguments, control and behavior&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o1">O1</a> · <a href="#o2">O2</a> · <a href="#o3">O3</a> · <a href="#o4">O4</a> · <a href="#o5">O5</a> · <a href="#o6">O6</a> · <a href="#o21">O21</a> · <a href="#o22">O22</a> · <a href="#o54">O54</a></p><p>Supported: Bulbasaur separates side-effect declarations, static assessment and explicit behavioral runs; MCP middleware and LangGraph show rules must reach execution. Regex does not prove read-only behavior, mock does not prove real effectiveness, and experimental APIs may change. Candidate: pin merged Bulbasaur code in an isolated development setup and compare allowed/excess/undeclared-effect cases, refusals, receipts and exact hashes; real execution needs separate isolation design. Compare CodeFlowMu admission/control and FCoP artifact/declaration/evidence contracts without assigning all policies to the protocol. Costs: mappings, sandbox and test cases. Not run. Classification: experiment candidate.</p><p>Discussion topic: Can a refusal receipt reconstruct the skill hash and actual effect mismatch?</p><p><span id="a2"></span></p><h3 id="a2-authorization-cannot-be-inferred-from-inherited-conversation-or-defaults" tabindex="-1">A2 Authorization cannot be inferred from inherited conversation or defaults <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-authorization-cannot-be-inferred-from-inherited-conversation-or-defaults" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 Authorization cannot be inferred from inherited conversation or defaults&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o11">O11</a> · <a href="#o12">O12</a> · <a href="#o13">O13</a> · <a href="#o14">O14</a> · <a href="#o19">O19</a> · <a href="#o30">O30</a> · <a href="#o31">O31</a> · <a href="#o32">O32</a> · <a href="#o33">O33</a> · <a href="#o35">O35</a> · <a href="#o36">O36</a> · <a href="#o37">O37</a> · <a href="#o43">O43</a> · <a href="#o45">O45</a> · <a href="#o48">O48</a> · <a href="#o53">O53</a></p><p>Supported: child evidence, manual caller, installed connection, tenant external ID and reviewed PR head each have boundaries; team defaults remain subordinate to organizational policy. Local CodeFlowMu applicability is unverified. Candidate: revoke before a delayed call, manually run another person&#39;s routine, fork inherited history, and change PR head after phone approval; compare identity/object version/decision/effect. Evidence catch-up plus post-verdict checks are useful, while moving tokens from argv removes one exposure only. Compare FCoP delegation/approval linkage; accounts, credentials and sandbox enforcement belong to Runtime/adapters. Costs: versioning, authorization lookups and human recovery. Classification: watch/experiment candidate.</p><p>Discussion topic: After approval, which authority/object-version changes force revalidation?</p><p><span id="a3"></span></p><h3 id="a3-completion-connects-dispatch-consumption-acceptance-and-external-delivery" tabindex="-1">A3 Completion connects dispatch, consumption, acceptance and external delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-completion-connects-dispatch-consumption-acceptance-and-external-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 Completion connects dispatch, consumption, acceptance and external delivery&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o15">O15</a> · <a href="#o16">O16</a> · <a href="#o23">O23</a> · <a href="#o26">O26</a> · <a href="#o28">O28</a> · <a href="#o38">O38</a> · <a href="#o39">O39</a> · <a href="#o44">O44</a> · <a href="#o46">O46</a> · <a href="#o48">O48</a> · <a href="#o51">O51</a> · <a href="#o55">O55</a></p><p>Supported: child replies can be lost on interruption, agent messages can look user-authored, tasks can complete before PR merge, and verifiers can false-pass. Local applicability remains untested. Priority candidate: research→implementation→independent acceptance with parent interruption, late child completion, synthetic human rejection, closed-unmerged PRs and verifier false positives; check dispatch, artifact hash/ID, consumption and acceptance receipts separately. Compare Paperclip external-fact gates with OpenHands narrow-question judging, whose mainline caller is still absent. FCoP concerns task/artifact/provenance/acceptance linkage; Runtime owns waiting, locks and dispatch. Costs: fault injection, controls and remote checks. Classification: high-value experiment candidate.</p><p>Discussion topic: How is it proven that independent review consumed the exact delivered version?</p><p><span id="a4"></span></p><h3 id="a4-recovery-distinguishes-session-turn-settlement-and-resource-release" tabindex="-1">A4 Recovery distinguishes session, turn, settlement and resource release <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-recovery-distinguishes-session-turn-settlement-and-resource-release" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 Recovery distinguishes session, turn, settlement and resource release&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o17">O17</a> · <a href="#o18">O18</a> · <a href="#o20">O20</a> · <a href="#o27">O27</a> · <a href="#o29">O29</a> · <a href="#o34">O34</a> · <a href="#o38">O38</a> · <a href="#o42">O42</a> · <a href="#o47">O47</a> · <a href="#o49">O49</a></p><p>Supported: reserve space does not guarantee turn continuation; terminal runs may still settle; HTTP200 is not a valid control response by itself; caller timeout does not prove worker termination. Extend recovery candidates with full-disk same-session continuation, lock sweep during usage waiting, idle worker death and waiter storms; measure duplicate effects, lost receipts, leaks and human waiting. Preserve partial-write/not-rolled-back migration states. Compare recoverable state/evidence at FCoP; pools, leases, disk, retries and resource reclamation at Runtime. Costs: controlled faults and reliable effect stubs. No local results. Classification: experiment/recovery reference.</p><p>Discussion topic: What independently proves execution and resource termination after a timeout?</p><p><span id="a5"></span></p><h3 id="a5-memory-and-spend-controls-need-lifecycle-and-subject-checks" tabindex="-1">A5 Memory and spend controls need lifecycle and subject checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-memory-and-spend-controls-need-lifecycle-and-subject-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 Memory and spend controls need lifecycle and subject checks&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o24">O24</a> · <a href="#o25">O25</a> · <a href="#o26">O26</a> · <a href="#o29">O29</a> · <a href="#o42">O42</a> · <a href="#o50">O50</a> · <a href="#o52">O52</a> · <a href="#o53">O53</a></p><p>Supported: default CrewAI storage is removed at exit, shared default IDs mixed runs, async clients could inherit closed loops, and own key budgets can replace defaults. Configuration names alone do not prove persistence/isolation/hard caps. Trial candidates: backed-up Chroma versus restart/two-process/resume behavior and separate user/key budgets, checking subjects and durability without migrating production data. Compare role memory, user spend and routing separately; vector storage/gateway billing is not FCoP&#39;s job. Costs: re-embedding, storage services, connections and model use. Classification: trial candidate; no installation/upgrade performed.</p><p>Discussion topic: What constraints remain with user-editable defaults and multiple workers?</p><p><span id="a6"></span></p><h3 id="a6-protocol-research-separates-messages-artifacts-events-and-identity" tabindex="-1">A6 Protocol research separates messages, artifacts, events and identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-protocol-research-separates-messages-artifacts-events-and-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 Protocol research separates messages, artifacts, events and identity&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o4">O4</a> · <a href="#o5">O5</a> · <a href="#o6">O6</a> · <a href="#o7">O7</a> · <a href="#o8">O8</a> · <a href="#o22">O22</a> · <a href="#o40">O40</a> · <a href="#o44">O44</a> · <a href="#o46">O46</a> · <a href="#o54">O54</a> · <a href="#o56">O56</a> · <a href="#o57">O57</a></p><p>Supported: MCP extension requests, repository-gated GitHub artifacts, CLI event waiting and capability-negotiated Orca mail address distinct layers; Dispatch-changing messages retain home authority. Compare task/message/artifact identity, state authority, versions and evidence contracts with FCoP instead of labeling every agent protocol a same-layer rival. Candidate: offline reordered/duplicate/old-capability messages, artifact IDs and UTF-8 chunks; try CLI waiting after preview access. Exactly-once, gap recovery and full host interoperability remain unverified. Costs: persisted adapter state, compensation and compatibility. Classification: complementary-protocol reference/experiment candidate.</p><p>Discussion topic: Who may mutate task state after cross-host message delivery?</p><p><span id="a7"></span></p><h3 id="a7-trial-mechanisms-before-concluding-overall-product-maturity" tabindex="-1">A7 Trial mechanisms before concluding overall product maturity <a class="header-anchor" href="#a7-trial-mechanisms-before-concluding-overall-product-maturity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A7 Trial mechanisms before concluding overall product maturity&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o9">O9</a> · <a href="#o10">O10</a> · <a href="#o18">O18</a> · <a href="#o25">O25</a> · <a href="#o28">O28</a> · <a href="#o29">O29</a> · <a href="#o30">O30</a> · <a href="#o32">O32</a> · <a href="#o34">O34</a> · <a href="#o35">O35</a> · <a href="#o36">O36</a> · <a href="#o37">O37</a> · <a href="#o38">O38</a> · <a href="#o39">O39</a> · <a href="#o40">O40</a> · <a href="#o41">O41</a> · <a href="#o42">O42</a> · <a href="#o43">O43</a> · <a href="#o44">O44</a> · <a href="#o45">O45</a> · <a href="#o46">O46</a> · <a href="#o47">O47</a> · <a href="#o56">O56</a></p><p>Judgment: Bulbasaur is a priority skill-admission/evaluation candidate (Apache-2.0). Paperclip is a delivery/recovery candidate (MIT), pinned to versions containing the target merges rather than assuming post-release fixes are packaged. Orca has high mobile-approval/cross-host/collaboration learning value and increased attention, retaining second-circle placement; root LICENSE retrieval failed, pending clarification before trials. Verified root MIT licenses support Beads/Orkas task/migration and Chinese-output candidates. Copilot team/connector mechanisms increase enterprise-product attention under plan/policy/preview limits. Radar circles unchanged; isolated fixes do not establish overall maturity. No installation, phone/Windows, signing/rollback or exhaustive commercial-boundary acceptance. Classification: ordered trial candidates, no development dispatch.</p><p>Discussion topic: Can each maturity claim be accepted against one exact delivered version?</p><h2 id="cross-project-synthesis-disposition-and-dual-source-coverage" tabindex="-1">Cross-project synthesis, disposition and dual-source coverage <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-synthesis-disposition-and-dual-source-coverage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project synthesis, disposition and dual-source coverage&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Prioritize A1/A3/A4 as experiment candidates, A2 for authority-boundary comparison, A5 for upgrade/continuity trials, A6 for complementary protocols, and A7 for competitor trial ordering. None was executed or establishes a local defect, validated mechanism, article or development assignment. Only discussion topics were retained; no external comments were posted.</p><p>GitHub checks covered commits, Issues/PR and releases on original entries, with release-history/selected issue backfill, selected PRs, skill/API documentation and licenses. Of 264 source/type checks, 229 completed, 32 retain pagination gaps, and three TSA endpoints were inaccessible. Only complete checks advance baselines. The Superset redirect was resolved by matching repository ID 1080370450 to ParadevAI/Paradev; follow-up did not rename/replace Registry entries or close historical pagination. Codex large release queries failed; a smaller query succeeded with pagination still incomplete.</p><p>The second source type checked Cursor changelog, the MCP official blog, GitHub changelog and three November 18 official announcements. Cursor/MCP latest entries remain November 6/11, not counted new. A five-author homepage expansion returned no result during an extended wait and was terminated as incomplete without advancing baselines. This is not an exhaustive sweep of 47 researchers, X/replies, papers, Discussions or installation/architecture/commercial boundaries. Apache-2.0 for Bulbasaur and root MIT for Paperclip/Beads/Orkas were verified; Orca root LICENSE retrieval failed and its applicable license remains pending. Person/repository relationships remain many-to-many; the Mansura project is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact, and the Chinese name is 赵越.</p><p>New releases count as delivery changes; old merges/open PRs are not recast as daily new events. CrewAI #9324 only explains this release boundary. Upstream tests do not replace local production-path validation. Only the two daily sources and two indices change, without research/runtime/**, business lifecycle, entry components or layout edits. Website publication/acceptance is recorded separately and in chat.</p>',330)])])}const m=a(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
